\begin{exercise}
\label{prob:paraboloid-isotropic-one-point}
\dcref{ch8:8-5}

Let $S \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3$ be the paraboloid given by $z = x^2 + y^2$, with the induced metric. Prove that $S$ is isotropic at only one point. (Used on p. 56.)
\end{exercise}

